  "story": "A city's rail map lists, for every station, the stations you can reach with one direct ride. Some rides only run one way, some lines loop back on themselves, and some stations are cut off from the rest. Stations are numbered from 0. Starting at one station, what is the smallest number of rides needed to arrive at the goal? Staying where you are takes 0 rides. If the goal cannot be reached at all, report -1.",
